      "writtenOn": "2021-06-22T02:36:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How does this deal with the fact that the different IpServers do not hear about the upstream change at the same time? When the upstream changes, IPv6TetheringCoordinator does:\n\n    private void updateIPv6TetheringInterfaces() {\n        for (IpServer ipServer : mNotifyList) {\n            final LinkProperties lp \u003d getInterfaceIPv6LinkProperties(ipServer);\n            ipServer.sendMessage(IpServer.CMD_IPV6_TETHER_UPDATE, getTtlAdjustment(), 0, lp);\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n\nwhich means that the IpServers only hear about the change one by one.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 232,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 232,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "f66792f70625ca4cd9701265f0436351c9af50ce",
